symmetry of (x - 1)^2:
  neither even nor odd
  not even: f(x) = 0, f(-x) = 4 at x = 1
  not odd: f(x) = 0, f(-x) = 4 at x = 1
  checked numerically at 2000 points of [-10, 10]
  symmetric about the line x = 1: f(c + h) = f(c - h) (checked numerically at 200 h up to 10)
