> is sin(2x) periodic?
  ucas: it(x) = sin(2*x)
  ucas: periodic it
periodic it:
  yes: fundamental period pi ≈ 3.141592654
  proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)
