  discriminant B^2 - 4AC = 4 (hyperbolic); determinant of the 3x3 matrix 1 (non-degenerate)
  hyperbola: centre (0, 0), asymptotes y = -x and y = x
  [coefficients by evaluation at 9 points, the form checked at 30 more: numeric]
  symmetric about: the y-axis, the x-axis, the origin [numeric, 40 points]
> what kind of equation is y'' + y = 0?
  ucas: identify y'' + y = 0
identify y'' + y = 0:
  an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)
  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]
  homogeneous
  constant coefficients (and autonomous)
  characteristic equation: r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i
  homogeneous solutions: y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)
  autonomous: the independent variable does not appear explicitly
  solved for the highest derivative: y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)
> classify y' = t*y
  ucas: identify y' = t*y
identify y' = t*y:
  an ordinary differential equation of order 1 in y(t)
  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]
  homogeneous
  variable coefficients (they depend on t)
  not autonomous: it depends on the independent variable explicitly
  first order: y' = t*y
  separable: yes, g = p(t) q(y) [numeric, 40 point pairs: g(t1, y1) g(t2, y2) = g(t1, y2) g(t2, y1)]
  exact (M + N y' = 0 with M = -(t*y), N = 1): no [numeric: dM/dy - dN/dt = -t]
  solved for the highest derivative: y' = t*y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)
> what type of function is x^3 - x?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - x
  ucas: identify it
identify it:
  it(x: real) = x^3 - x
  -> real
  polynomial of degree 3 (cubic), leading coefficient 1
  factored over the reals: x(x + 1)(x - 1)
  domain: all real x [proved: no partial operation]
  continuous on its domain [proved: continuous operations]
  parity: odd: f(-x) = -f(x) [proved]
  periodic: no [proved]
  monotonic: not monotonic (3 intervals of monotonicity) [proved]
  neither convex nor concave, inflection at 0 [proved]
  unbounded above and below [proved]
  values on [-10, 10]: from -990 to 990 [numeric]
  injective: no, f(-1.141929725) = f(0.4226497308) = -0.3471506281 [witness]
  zeros: 3 (-1, 0, 1) [proved]
  (numeric results are for [-10, 10]: x has no range; each property has its own command)
