identify it:
  it(x: real) = exp(-x^2)
  -> real
  transcendental: exponential
  domain: all real x [proved: no partial operation]
  continuous on its domain [proved: continuous operations]
  parity: even: f(-x) = f(x) [proved]
  periodic: no [numeric]
  monotonic: not monotonic (2 intervals of monotonicity) [numeric]
  neither convex nor concave, inflection at -0.7071067812, 0.7071067812 [numeric]
  bounded [proved]
  values on [-10, 10]: from 3.720075976e-44 to 1 [numeric]
  injective: no, f(-1) = f(1) = 0.3678794412 [witness]
  zeros: 0 [numeric]
  asymptotes: y = 0 (x -> ±inf) [numeric]
  (numeric results are for [-10, 10]: x has no range; each property has its own command)
> classify the function sin(x)/x
  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)/x
  ucas: identify it
identify it:
  it(x: real) = sin(x)/x
  -> real
  transcendental: trigonometric, with quotients
  domain: all real x except x = 0 [numeric]
  discontinuous at x = 0 (removable) [numeric]
  parity: even: f(-x) = f(x) [proved]
  periodic: no [numeric]
  monotonic: not monotonic (6 intervals of monotonicity) [numeric]
  neither convex nor concave, inflection at -9.205840143, -5.940369991, -2.081575978, ... [numeric]
  bounded [numeric]
  values on [-10, 10]: from -0.2172336282 to 0.9999998333 [numeric]
  injective: no, f(-8.828461939) = f(-6.725251837) = 0.06361222759 [witness]
  zeros: 6 (-9.424777961 (~-3*pi), -6.283185307 (~-2*pi), -3.141592654 (~-pi), 3.141592654 (~pi), 6.283185307 (~2*pi), 9.424777961 (~3*pi)) [numeric]
  asymptotes: y = 0 (x -> ±inf) [numeric]
  (numeric results are for [-10, 10]: x has no range; each property has its own command)
> is u8(x + 1) monotonic for an unsigned byte x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = u8(x + 1)
  ucas: monotonic it
monotonic it:
  not monotonic on 0..255
  maximal intervals of monotonicity:
    x in 0..254: increasing
    x in 254..255: decreasing
  witness: x = 0 < x = 1 but f(0) = 1 < f(1) = 2 (not decreasing)
  witness: x = 254 < x = 255 but f(254) = 255 > f(255) = 0 (not increasing)
  note: without wrapping (as int) it is strictly increasing; the machine type wraps: f(254) = 255, f(255) = 0
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points (forward difference f(x+1) - f(x))
